Cell["\<\
With r=q0 and ell=q0-q4, q0/q1 pinch r-plus with width delta^4, q4/q5 pinch \
ell-plus with width delta^4, and q2/q3 pinch ell-minus with width delta. Both \
transverse widths scale as delta^2. Thus r has local widths (4,0,2) and ell \
has widths (4,1,2), giving two-loop measure power 4D+1. The denominator \
powers sum to 21.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6b224b8f-b99f-4cf4-a55d-bba47f984a11"],

Cell["\<\
In parameter space use A=x2-X34hat^(-1) delta^3 x3 and B=x1 x4-x0 x5. The HRF \
gap gives wt(A)=0 while wt(B)=-8. Four tangential coordinates contribute -16 \
and the Jacobian -1/x0 contributes +4, so the measure has power -20. The \
resolved LP polynomial of weight -8 contributes delta^(4D).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"85c377d5-79bd-47b6-af9d-160bcf2f1c09"],

